# Line-ending policy.
#
# `z:\` is an SMB mount of the NAS filesystem that Docker builds from directly, and
# this repo is edited from Windows where core.autocrlf=true. Without these rules a
# checkout rewrites LF→CRLF *in place* on the live NAS files: nginx mostly tolerates
# CRLF, but a CRLF shebang breaks shell scripts outright.
#
# Anything consumed by Linux (configs, scripts, Dockerfiles) is pinned to LF.

* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.env       text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.h5  binary
*.pkl binary
*.joblib binary
